Use this tool to read or set Nest thermostat state.

Pass any combination of these state fields to set them. The tool applies
each present field; omit a field to leave it unchanged. Pass nothing to
read current state.

State fields (all optional):
  - `mode`               — `HEAT`, `COOL`, `HEATCOOL`, or `OFF`. Bare uppercase.
  - `target_temperature` — Fahrenheit number (e.g. 75).
  - `fan_mode`           — `ON`, `AUTO`, or `OFF`.
  - `eco_enabled`        — true/false. Eco-mode toggle.

Selector (optional):
  - `device_id` — target a specific thermostat. Omit for default.

Examples of correct shape:
  Change setpoint:           `{ "target_temperature": 75 }`
  Switch to cooling at 72:   `{ "mode": "COOL", "target_temperature": 72 }`
  Read current state:        `{}`
